Hedge-shaping, and dreams seem to come up a good deal.<br /> <br /> A quick piece of advice: Start with preludes for the PCs. I am sometimes still surprised to note how things we set up in preludes influence things years later.<br /> <br /> And even if it doesn't have to be said, I'll add: Use everything around you. Look for ways you can convert just about anything into a Keeper, a hobgoblin, a changeling, a Durance, and so on. The concepts don't have to look or sound like stereotypical fairy tale fodder to become fairy tale fodder in Changeling; that is one of the strongest aspects of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}